# Testing Rules

## Setup
- Vitest + jsdom + React Testing Library; config in `vitest.config.ts`.
- Tests live in `src/test/` (not beside the source), named `*.test.ts(x)`.
- `src/test/setup.ts` primes the generated player data and jest-dom matchers.
- Globals (`describe`/`it`/`expect`) are enabled, but existing files import them
  from `vitest` explicitly — follow that.
- `npm run test:fast` skips the long season/longevity suites listed in
  `SLOW_SUITES` (`vitest.config.ts`); `npm run test` runs everything (CI).
  Run a single file with `npx vitest run src/test/<file>`.

## What to test
- Every behaviour change gets a test that FAILS without the change.
- Slice actions and pure utils first; components for user-visible behaviour.
- Seed or stub randomness (`withSeededRandom` in `src/test/helpers/seasonFixtures.ts`,
  or `vi.spyOn(Math, 'random')`) so a test cannot pass by luck.
- Build fixtures with `src/test/helpers/seasonFixtures.ts` rather than
  hand-rolling clubs and players.
- Long loops that `await` must yield to the timer phase — see
  `src/test/helpers/eventLoop.ts`.

## Don'ts
- Don't test `src/components/ui/` — third-party primitives.
- No snapshot tests.
- Don't assert on CSS classes; assert behaviour and content.
